  "title": "The moves force a groupoid, and counting sees only finite quotients",
  "subject": "Which counting laws with composite labels survive the moves of three-dimensional triangulations, and what they see",
  "conclusion": "On ordered triangulations, a counting law whose long edge is a function of the two short edges survives the moves exactly when its working triangles form a finite groupoid with equal component values; the objects are the idempotent labels. Its count is a sum of |Hom(pi1(M), G)|/|G|, so such laws see a three-manifold only through the finite quotients of its fundamental group.",
